  "summary": "A solenoid valve opens and closes electrically. In this normally-closed, pilot-operated design the coil lifts a small plunger, which opens a pilot orifice; pressure above the diaphragm bleeds away and line pressure lifts the diaphragm off the main seat. De-energising the coil lets the spring push the plunger back and the valve closes. A minimum pressure difference is needed to operate.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Automated on/off valve",
    "type": "2/2-way normally closed, servo (pilot) operated diaphragm"
  },
